course: dictionary
lesson: 16133
title: Whitewashed: paint, cover-ups and lost games
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Whitewashed has three meanings, so look at the words around it to find the right one. «Mole grabbed his brush and whitewashed the walls of his little home.» The brush and the walls tell you it means painted with whitewash.
explain: Whitewash is a cheap white paint made from lime and water. It is used on the walls of cottages and farms. «The farm walls were whitewashed every spring.» Here the clue is walls, so the paint meaning fits.
explain: Adults also use whitewashed to mean covered up. «The report was whitewashed, so the mistakes were never found.» The clue is mistakes never found: someone hid the truth. In sport, «The team was whitewashed in the series» means the team lost every game.
fact: Whitewashed is the past form of whitewash.
fact: «Whitewashed» can mean painted with cheap white paint made of lime and water.
fact: «Whitewashed» can also mean covered up, so the truth is hidden.
fact: In sport, «whitewashed» means losing every game in a series.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Mole whitewashes his little home during spring-cleaning, until he throws down his brush.
exercise: «Mole spent the morning whitewashing his little home.» What does whitewashing mean here? | Hiding the truth from his friends | Losing a game | *Painting the walls with cheap white paint | Cleaning the floor with soap
exercise: «The report was whitewashed, so the mistakes never came to light.» What does whitewashed mean? | Painted bright red | *Covered up, hiding the truth | Left out in the rain | Made clean and new
exercise: «The team was whitewashed in every match of the series.» In sport, what does this mean? | They played in the rain | *They lost every match in the series | They won every match | They were given a new kit
test: In Tom Sawyer, Tom tricks his friends into whitewashing a fence. What job are they doing? | Washing a dog in the river | *Painting a fence with whitewash | Writing a report for the teacher | Climbing a tall tree
test: «The news story was whitewashed, and the real problem was never mentioned.» What does this suggest? | *The truth was hidden | The story was painted a new colour | The story was very long | The problem was solved quickly
exam: Which sentence uses whitewashed to mean covered up? | Tom and his friends whitewashed the fence | The cottage walls were freshly whitewashed | Mole's little home was whitewashed in spring | *The inquiry was whitewashed, so the truth never came out
